<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 7-yr govt bond price down at 103.64 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary 7-yr govt bond price down at 103.64 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price of Hungary's seven-year government bonds was set by auction at 103.64 percent of the face value, down from 103.9 percent at an auction on November 21, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BONDS OF THE 2003/F SERIES</p>
<p>    Issue date		  October 17, 1996</p>
<p>    Total on offer	    11,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     11,054.38 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   11,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		12,100 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum price		     103.40 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     103.64 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price		     104.27 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - The bond bears a floating interest, calculated on March 20 and September 20 every year adding three percent to year-on-year consumer inflation. The interest is paid once a year, on September 24. The starting interest is 25.9 percent.</p>
</text>
